libcarmen SDK (@SDK_VERSION@, @SDK_OS@ @SDK_ARCH@, @SDK_FLAVOR@)

A relocatable developer SDK for linking your own C, FFI, or WebAssembly
program against libcarmen. Unpack this folder anywhere; no install prefix
is baked into the paths below (pkg-config and CMake resolve them relative
to this location).

Layout:

  include/carmen/       public headers (#include <carmen/carmen.h>)
  lib/                  the libcarmen library (see flavor below)
  lib/pkgconfig/        carmen.pc (relocatable pkg-config file)
  lib/cmake/carmen/     CMake package config for find_package(carmen)
                        (shipped in the CMake-built SDK archive)

Consume it one of these three ways (use <prefix> = this folder):

1. Raw compiler flags -- static:

      cc my_game.c -I<prefix>/include -L<prefix>/lib -lcarmen -lm -o my_game

   libcarmen uses the C math library; when linking the static archive you
   must pass -lm explicitly (the shared library already records it).

2. pkg-config:

      PKG_CONFIG_PATH=<prefix>/lib/pkgconfig cc my_game.c \
          $(pkg-config --cflags --libs carmen) -o my_game

   For the static archive pass --static so pkg-config also emits -lm:

      pkg-config --static --cflags --libs carmen

3. CMake find_package (CMake-built SDK only):

      find_package(carmen REQUIRED)
      add_executable(my_game my_game.c)
      target_link_libraries(my_game PRIVATE carmen::carmen)

   Point CMake at this SDK with -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=<prefix>.

If you use the shared library, keep libcarmen.<*>.{dylib,so} on the
runtime library search path; this SDK ships the soname and dev symlinks
next to the real file so both compile-time and run-time names resolve.

